P77 — Verify demand-driven Sync presentation reads. (
    @park-p77: 0,
    is #task,
    #park-performance-task,
    #park-stage-a1,
    #part-of @park-dev-05-feature-costs-and-scaling: 13,
    #park-workflow @park-development-cycle
) { r_349MAGE5FADNJ50X348MCC7604
**Current workflow:** [Development cycle](record:r_043BC6V4K9R3X6E9E4TZP3P6J0). **Resume state:** [Current checkpoint](record:r_2KDK4ZZZJNBEK0J23TFNQAZF9Y).

**Implementation is complete for the selected Sync presentation family; verification only.** Hidden plugin-catalog and pending-offer panels retire their read-only watcher through the shared snapshot-demand helper. Existing output, preview, portal, ancestor-display and suppression rules determine demand; reveal creates a fresh immediate snapshot worker. Action jobs, transfers, directory sync and automation retain their lifetime. Blob-transfer snapshots also serve non-UI consumers and are deliberately outside this display-only gate. Their newly shared latest/presented snapshots and retained transfer controls are implemented separately, with BLOB-PRESENTATION-VERIFY in Overhaul.md owning that verification. Sync history now uses the existing shared deadline owner rather than a permanent polling timer; its wake, reply and retry checks remain under SYNC-DEMAND-VERIFY. Directory Sync now owns direct subscription/save reply routes, reserves request capacity before query construction, retains unchanged Protein choice buttons and skips identical enabled/status writes. SYNC-DEMAND-VERIFY also owns multi-owner/late-reply/cleanup, draft, accessible-switch and retained-choice checks; this is implemented source, not another coding task.

Catalog and pending-offer UI now share immutable snapshot handles with their workers and use the retained-children family for their lists. Status-only catalog changes retain controls; cross-row move/invitation and retry-provider inputs participate in invalidation. Their shared refresh owner skips forecast-only notices and missed polling bursts while preserving initial/periodic/general reads. Settings opening borrows catalog metadata instead of copying the whole catalog/contribution. These source reductions are also implemented and await SYNC-DEMAND-VERIFY; no runtime result is claimed.

The backend plugin catalog now reads enabled approvals once, derives dependency availability from one installed-package snapshot with indexed linear propagation, and reuses its enabled-ID set for diagnostics and bindings. Real plugin execution still uses the original fresh authorization reader; catalog data grants no execution authority.

**Why:** hidden panels should not poll/read/rebuild display-only state, and one catalog request should not clone the entire package list and query the same dependency graph per package. **Verify:** SYNC-DEMAND-VERIFY in [Overhaul.md](Overhaul.md) owns hidden/revealed/multiple panels, output/preview/portal demand, close/reopen, drafts and in-flight actions, errors/retry, absent/changed/disabled dependency chains and cycles, and fresh execution authorization after catalog publication. Compare watcher/read/graph counts, complete query waits, allocation/memory and input/CPU costs. No tests, build or measurements have run for these reductions.

} r_349MAGE5FADNJ50X348MCC7604

