P128 — Verify retained terminal and Command output. (
    @park-p128: 0,
    is #task,
    #park-performance-task,
    #park-stage-a1,
    #part-of @park-dev-05-feature-costs-and-scaling: 25,
    #park-workflow @park-development-cycle
) { r_5ZXJ3Y0TZEG0T3PDAH61X596QJ
**Status — implemented, verification pending (2026-11-15).** Terminal rows/runs now use shared retained presentation. The worker binds typed Wasm exports once, shares immutable frames, skips unchanged screen publications while preserving input/reply wakes, and maintains its queued byte count. Command history avoids its extra full-run reconciliation clone, repeated membership scans and unchanged header/order writes; relevant message filtering and borrowed unchanged cwd reads avoid extra consumer work. Original notifications, output bytes/history, limits, authorization and cancellation remain.

**Evidence:** [Overhaul.md — source-only terminal and Command output](Overhaul.md#source-only-terminal-and-command-output--2026-11-15). No build, test or measurement was run. Full Wasm frame extraction and the existing per-command processing boundary are unchanged; their remaining cost is not assumed to be unnecessary.

**Why:** A fast local output stream must not make unrelated input late through repeated entity construction, export lookup, history copying or redundant publications.

**Remaining verification:** TERMINAL-VERIFY in Overhaul.md owns exact output/Unicode/style/cursor/background checks, typed ABI compatibility, ordered playback and live stdin, identical-frame reply wakeups, exit/error/cancellation/removal, multiple instances and another editor under the same sustained stream. Compare complete response and CPU/memory as well as the new snapshot/presentation/history scopes and reuse/publication counters. Any remaining queue/service-bound change needs evidence of its owner; do not add a second terminal implementation, polling or lost output to close the task.

**Current workflow:** [Development cycle](record:r_043BC6V4K9R3X6E9E4TZP3P6J0). The current phase remains source-only.
} r_5ZXJ3Y0TZEG0T3PDAH61X596QJ

