**Status — implemented, verification pending (2026-11-15).** File Explorer keeps its existing visible-range limit and now reconciles buttons through the shared retained-children family. Overlapping rows retain identity; changed selection, placement and caption inputs update only their owned fields. Source generation and full row/action identity prevent slot reuse for a different file. Root controls and their sibling order remain explicit.

Directory completions defer accumulated sorting to one pass per changed directory before model preparation, reusing the worker's existing sorted batches. Search results own the row model directly, removing the second full-result copy; unused directory prefetch/sorting waits until the directory view is needed again. Existing workers, cancellation, watchers and source/scope checks remain. Complete directory flattening still occurs; this is not a second virtualization framework or full tree-model incrementality.

**Still to verify:** Follow EXPLORER-VERIFY in Overhaul.md for tree/grid/search, overlapping roots, keyboard/scroll reveal, selection, metadata updates, replacement/held input, cancellation and exact sorted contents. Compare creation/retention, sort/model costs and memory together, including all-changing views.

**Why:** Scrolling one row or changing selection should not reconstruct every visible control, and one presentation wave should not repeatedly prepare the same listing.

**Current instruction:** source changes only. Do not run checks, compile, measure, ship or restart from this Record. Use [Overhaul.md](Overhaul.md#remaining-acceptance-obligations) and [the checkpoint](record:r_2KDK4ZZZJNBEK0J23TFNQAZF9Y); verification resumes only when authorized. Quantity remains zero because implementation is not a performance pass.

} r_7G4HJRCVP9TZW0S1XS934HDWPQ

